hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20970","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Ribi ibn Hirash from Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah, brother of Aishah by her mother, that he saw in what the sleeper sees as if he passed by a group of Jews and said: Who are you. They said: We are the Jews. He said: You are the people were it not that you claim Uzayr is the son of Allah. The Jews said: And you are the people were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. Then he passed by a group of Christians and said: Who are you. They said: We are the Christians. He said: You are the people were it not that you say: The Messiah is the son of Allah. They said: And you are the people were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. In the morning he told it to whom he told, then came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him. He said: Did you tell it to anyone. Affan said: He said: Yes. When they prayed he addressed them, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Tufayl saw a vision and told it to whom he told of you, and you used to say a word shyness from you prevented me from forbidding you from it. He said: Do not say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills."
